  "id": "DrugBank_DB00180 - MONDO_4784",
  "verbalization": "Flunisolide is associated with Allergic Asthma through a series of indications that collectively support its potential repurposing. The evidence suggests that Flunisolide may exert a therapeutic effect on allergic asthma via multiple pathways, including interactions with the immune system and bronchoconstriction. The indication of Asthma to Reproterol and Ibudilast, both of which are linked to Allergic Asthma, indicates that Flunisolide may influence the disease process through mechanisms that are not directly known. The presence of multiple pathways involving different mediators of allergic asthma suggests that Flunisolide could act through a broader range of biological processes, potentially modulating inflammatory responses and airway constriction. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship and underscores the need for further mechanistic investigation to clarify the exact mode of action.",
